     fhir:Narrative.div "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><div xml:lang=\"en\" lang=\"en\"><hr/><p><b>English</b></p><hr/><p class=\"res-header-id\"><b>Generated Narrative: CodeSystem KGRecommendationKind</b></p><a name=\"KGRecommendationKind\"> </a><a name=\"hcKGRecommendationKind\"> </a><p>This case-sensitive code system <code>http://smart.who.int/base/CodeSystem/KGRecommendationKind</code> defines the following codes:</p><table class=\"codes\"><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><b>Code</b></td><td><b>Display</b></td><td><b>Definition</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">recommendation<a name=\"KGRecommendationKind-recommendation\"> </a></td><td>Recommendation</td><td>A graded recommendation, with a direction and a strength. Handbook §10.4.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">context-specific<a name=\"KGRecommendationKind-context-specific\"> </a></td><td>Context specific</td><td>Recommended only in specified contexts or settings, stated in the recommendation. ANC guideline (2016) Table 1, verified.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">research-context<a name=\"KGRecommendationKind-research-context\"> </a></td><td>Research context</td><td>Recommended only in the context of rigorous research. ANC guideline (2016) Table 1, verified.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">good-practice-statement<a name=\"KGRecommendationKind-good-practice-statement\"> </a></td><td>Good practice statement</td><td>An ungraded statement whose benefit is so clear that grading the evidence is not a useful exercise. Carries no strength or certainty. Guyatt et al. 2016.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">no-recommendation<a name=\"KGRecommendationKind-no-recommendation\"> </a></td><td>No recommendation</td><td>\"No recommendation can be made because…\" — the guideline development group decided the evidence could not support one. Handbook §10.7. Distinct from very-low certainty: absent evidence and weak evidence are different findings.</td></tr></table></div><div xml:lang=\"fr\" lang=\"fr\"><hr/><p><b>French</b></p><hr/><p class=\"res-header-id\"><b>Narratif généré : CodeSystem KGRecommendationKind</b></p><a name=\"fr-KGRecommendationKind\"> </a><a name=\"fr-hcKGRecommendationKind\"> </a><p>This case-sensitive code system <code>http://smart.who.int/base/CodeSystem/KGRecommendationKind</code> defines the following codes:</p><table class=\"codes\"><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><b>Code</b></td><td><b>Affichage</b></td><td><b>Définition</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">recommendation<a name=\"fr-KGRecommendationKind-recommendation\"> </a></td><td>Recommendation</td><td>A graded recommendation, with a direction and a strength. Handbook §10.4.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">context-specific<a name=\"fr-KGRecommendationKind-context-specific\"> </a></td><td>Context specific</td><td>Recommended only in specified contexts or settings, stated in the recommendation. ANC guideline (2016) Table 1, verified.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">research-context<a name=\"fr-KGRecommendationKind-research-context\"> </a></td><td>Research context</td><td>Recommended only in the context of rigorous research. ANC guideline (2016) Table 1, verified.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">good-practice-statement<a name=\"fr-KGRecommendationKind-good-practice-statement\"> </a></td><td>Good practice statement</td><td>An ungraded statement whose benefit is so clear that grading the evidence is not a useful exercise. Carries no strength or certainty. Guyatt et al. 2016.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">no-recommendation<a name=\"fr-KGRecommendationKind-no-recommendation\"> </a></td><td>No recommendation</td><td>\"No recommendation can be made because…\" — the guideline development group decided the evidence could not support one. Handbook §10.7. Distinct from very-low certainty: absent evidence and weak evidence are different findings.</td></tr></tabl